{"name":"Rising Tide","hex":"#cbd6d8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rising","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of rise"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rebellion.","The act of something that rises."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rising"},{"term":"tide","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The daily fluctuation in the level of the sea caused by the gravitational influence of the moon and the sun.","The associated flow of water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to float with the tide; to drive or carry with the tide or stream.","To carry over or through a problem or difficulty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tide"}],"entries":[{"title":"A rising tide lifts all boats","blocks":[{"text":"\"A rising tide lifts all boats\" is an aphorism associated with the idea that an improved economy will benefit all participants and that economic policy, particularly government economic policy, should therefore focus on broad economic efforts."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_rising_tide_lifts_all_boats","wikidata":"Q4660966"},{"title":"Rising Tide North America","blocks":[{"text":"Rising Tide North America is a grassroots network of groups and individuals in North America organizing action against the root causes of climate change."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rising_Tide_North_America","wikidata":"Q7336181"},{"title":"Rising Tide (Thesman novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Rising Tide (2003) is a historical young-adult novel by Jean Thesman and a sequel to her novel A Sea So Far (2001)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Rising_Tide_2003_Hardback_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rising_Tide_(Thesman_novel)","wikidata":"Q7336180"},{"title":"Tide","blocks":[{"text":"Tides are the periodic rise and fall of sea level resulting from t